Moreover I was also wondering if it's possible to extract from INLA the cross-validated posterior predictive distribution, i.e. pi(Y_i | y_-i). AFAIK the CPO values represent the cross-validated posterior predictive distribution evaluated at Y_i = y_i^obs while the PIT represent the Cumulative Distribution Function of the same distribution evaluated at y_i^obs.

I'm not sure if this is a reasonable question but I was wondering if it's possible to extract an estimation of the cross-validated posterior predictive distribution to implement alternative measures of PIT for count data.

Thank you very much for your help.
Kind regards
Andrea

